skills/umbrella/scripts/helpers.md:19:Stdout grammar: `EDGES_ADDED=<N>`, per-edge `EDGE_<j>_BLOCKER=<N>` / `EDGE_<j>_BLOCKED=<M>`, `EDGES_REJECTED_CYCLE=<N>`, `EDGES_SKIPPED_EXISTING=<N>` (already-present edges, including idempotent 422 already-exists responses per `add-blocked-by.sh:193-196`), `EDGES_SKIPPED_API_UNAVAILABLE=<N>` (repo-wide probe failure OR per-edge feature-missing 404 — both mean "the GitHub dependency surface was not usable here for this run"; **semantics intentionally preserved** by issue #728's fix — see `PROBE_FAILED` below for the cause disambiguator), `EDGES_FAILED=<N>` covers two categories: (a) per-edge **operational** failures — rate-limit, permission denied, ambiguous 404, other 4xx, 5xx, request-shape mismatches, blocker-id lookup failure, network — failures that do NOT match the feature-missing fingerprint; (b) per-edge **policy-driven** failures — `bound-exhausted`, set when the transitive `blocked_by` traversal hit `WIRE_DAG_TRAVERSAL_NODE_CAP` and the per-edge cycle-check loop's `CYCLE=false` answer cannot be trusted on a known-incomplete TSV (issue #718 fail-closed posture, voted 3-0 in the design-phase dialectic). `PROBE_FAILED=<0|1>` (issue #728) is a parse-only per-run flag distinguishing the two repo-wide-skip causes: `0` = confirmed feature-missing (probe got a fingerprinted 404) **OR** no probe attempted (e.g., `--no-backlinks` first-child path with empty `CHILDREN_FILE` — `probe_target` was empty, no probe ran, `PROBE_FAILED` stays at its initialization value); `1` = transient/operational probe failure (5xx + retry also failed, or HTTP response other than 2xx/fingerprinted-404). The retry policy is one network-only retry on `5xx` and empty-status (no HTTP response at all); `429`, other `4xx`, and `2xx`/fingerprinted-404 are single-attempt (clear HTTP responses are not transport blips). `BACKLINKS_POSTED=<N>`, `BACKLINKS_SKIPPED_EXISTING=<N>` (count of children whose existing back-link comment matching <code>Part of umbrella #${UMBRELLA} — </code> was detected in the comment stream; renamed from `BACKLINKS_SKIPPED_NATIVE` per #716 — see semantic migration note below).
skills/umbrella/scripts/helpers.md:72:The `/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}/dependencies/blocked_by` REST endpoint surface evolved during 2024-2026 (sub-issues vs blocked-by, REST vs GraphQL surfaces). `wire-dag` is fail-open by design for the wiring action: when the probe fails (whether feature-missing or transient), all proposed edges land in `EDGES_SKIPPED_API_UNAVAILABLE`. Issue #728 added a **three-way probe classification** to disambiguate the cause: `available` → wiring proceeds; `feature-missing` (fingerprinted 404) → wiring skipped, `PROBE_FAILED=0`; `probe-failed` (5xx-after-retry, no-status-after-retry, 429, or other non-fingerprinted 4xx) → wiring skipped, `PROBE_FAILED=1` and the new transient-probe stderr fires. In the **default mode** (no `--no-backlinks`), back-links via plain `gh issue comment` still proceed even when the probe fails on either path. In `--no-backlinks` mode (created-eq-1 bypass), the back-link loop is skipped regardless of probe outcome and stderr is mode-aware (see the wire-dag stderr contract above).
